# What EAS Build uploads for the phone app (apps/mobile, .github/workflows/mobile-release.yml). EAS reads this file only
# at the repository root, and it replaces every .gitignore. The app needs its own folder and @nexus/kit (packages/kit),
# so nothing else is uploaded: the app installs from its own package-lock.json, and the kit is a tsconfig path and a
# Metro watch folder with no dependencies.
# No pattern ends in "/": eas-cli matches each path without a trailing slash, so a directory-only pattern never matches
# the directory itself. Check a change with `eas build:inspect --stage archive`.
/*
!/apps
/apps/*
!/apps/mobile
!/packages
/packages/*
!/packages/kit

# The app's .gitignore, repeated because this file replaces it, and every .env file. EAS also uploads untracked files,
# and a local .env can hold a sign-in for a local Gateway.
node_modules
.expo
dist
web-build
expo-env.d.ts
.kotlin
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
.metro-health-check*
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
.DS_Store
*.pem
.env
.env.*
*.tsbuildinfo
/apps/mobile/ios
/apps/mobile/android
